      "accumulation_policy": "Sampling units are original observedsites within eachManagementstratum. A species is present exactly when its observed coverclass>0. For eachstratum,K_species is the numberofsiteswithpresence,andN is the numberofsitesinthatstratum,not sumsofcoverclasses. Compute expected numberofspecies encountered underuniform sampling without replacement at the common minimum numberofsites across strata. Also report its expected gain at oneadditionalsite onlyif thatdraw doesnot exceed the observedstratumsize;otherwise reportnull.",
      "inference_scope": "Conditional finite-observed-site expectation only. Ordinal coverclasses are not numbersofindividuals. Sites and species can be dependent;linearity ofthe expected coverage doesnot assume independent speciesoccurrences. No unseen habitat,spatial independence,causal management effect or future-site extrapolation is inferred.",
